  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence (experiment 1 of 10), the goal is to establish a strong performance reference and reduce uncertainty about whether the most expressive architecture is near-optimal. Config_003 combines all the most powerful design choices: multimodal (RNA+image), multiprofile (richer cellular context), scgpt (learned, nonlinear RNA encoder vs. linear PCA), imagenet_vit_l (large pretrained ViT vs. smaller ResNet50), transformer aggregation (more expressive than avgpool), and weighted fusion (learned channel weighting vs. simple concat). Testing this 'full-power' configuration first gives a high-ceiling baseline: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate individual components to identify which design choices are critical; if it underperforms, we immediately know to simplify. Under a tight 10-experiment budget, anchoring the search near the likely optimum and then exploring locally is more efficient than starting from a weak baseline and climbing."
}

